{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "ClientCommand",
  "description": "A command from a UI client to the runtime.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "description": "Ask the runtime for one best-effort prediction of the user's next prompt. The request is advisory UI chrome: it starts no task, persists no message, and may produce no event when there is insufficient context.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "request_prompt_suggestion"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Generate a one-shot recap after the UI has observed a post-turn idle window. The runtime may decline when the conversation is too short.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "request_away_summary"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Submit a user message; the runtime drives a turn in the given session.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "attachments": {
          "default": [],
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/AttachmentRef"
          }
        },
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "submit_message"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Steer the turn that is already running: the text is injected at the top of the next round instead of waiting for the turn to end.\n\nDistinct from queuing a follow-up (which `SubmitMessage` does while busy): a correction like \"actually use the other module\" is worthless once the work is finished. Ignored when no turn is running — the caller should submit normally in that case.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "steer_current_turn"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Run an explicit goal task. Unlike ordinary chat messages, this enables goal-mode completion (`update_goal`) in the agent loop.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "run_goal"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Run the Develop workflow on an explicit goal: `Analyze → Coding → Verify → Review`.\n\nDistinct from [`Self::RunGoal`] because it is a different product promise, not a different phrasing of the same one: the user is asking for the change to be investigated before it is written and read back after it is verified. An ordinary message never becomes one of these.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "run_develop"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Continue the session's interrupted logical task through the runtime's existing resume path, instead of starting a fresh turn.\n\nThe client sends this when the user expressed continuation intent (see [`crate::parse_continuation`]); the runtime remains the authority on whether a resumable task actually exists. When none does, the runtime falls back to the ordinary submit path, so a `ResumeTask` is never lost — it is either a resume or a normal message.\n\n`content` is the user's own text (for example `继续，但是先不要跑测试`): the runtime parses the amendment off it, preserving the original objective and adding the instruction, never replacing it.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "resume_task"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Import a file as an attachment; the runtime processes and stores it.\n\n`name` overrides the display name that would otherwise come from the file name. A terminal that answers Cmd+V on an image by writing a scratch file and pasting its path knows the file name is its own bookkeeping (`clipboard-2026-09-16-215212-CE7C9522.png`) and not something the user chose — only the client that made the gesture knows that, so only it can say so.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "path",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "default": null,
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "path": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "add_attachment"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Import an attachment from immutable base64-encoded bytes already read by a trusted client. This avoids reopening an ambient path after a security-sensitive upload or file-picker validation.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "data_base64",
        "name",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "data_base64": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "add_attachment_data"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Import an image from the system clipboard (spec §38.1).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "add_clipboard_image"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Retire this runtime once its current work has settled.\n\nOne mechanism covers both cases the caller cares about: an idle runtime drains instantly and exits, a busy one stops taking new work and exits when the work it already owns is done. The caller never polls for idleness and never kills anything — the runtime owns the drain, because only it knows what \"still working\" means.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "reason",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/RestartReason"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "shutdown_when_idle"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Cooperatively cancel the running turn (graceful; resumable).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "cancel_current_turn"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Escalate a cancel the user has already requested once.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "force_cancel_current_turn"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Cancel the logical task, not just the running turn.\n\nDistinct from [`Self::CancelCurrentTurn`]: that interrupts the current work window and leaves the task resumable, while this is the user saying the task itself is over. The runtime commits a terminal `cancelled` outcome, settles the goal, and refuses a later continuation — a `继续` must not silently reopen it.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "cancel_task"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Cancel ONE running delegated child of the session's turn. The child settles as cancelled; its parent turn keeps running.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "child_id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "child_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "cancel_child"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Stop ONE running tool call of the session's turn (for a command, its whole process tree). The call settles with its own stop outcome; the turn keeps running. Rejected when no such call is executing.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "call_id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "call_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ToolCallId"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "cancel_tool_call"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Resolve a pending permission request .",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "decision",
        "request_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "decision": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ApprovalDecision"
        },
        "request_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ApprovalId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "approval_decision"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Answer a pending clarification (spec §35). An empty answer means \"skip\".",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "answer",
        "request_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "answer": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "request_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ClarificationId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "answer_clarification"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Switch the model used for subsequent turns .",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "model",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "model": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ModelRef"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "select_model"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "The user's explicit \"use this model from now on\": switch the active session's model AND persist it as the user's default model for future sessions.\n\nDistinct from [`Self::SelectModel`] on purpose. Only this command carries the authority to rewrite the user's persisted configuration, because only an explicit user action does. Runtime fallbacks, provider failover, retries, temporary CLI/session overrides and internal routing MUST use [`Self::SelectModel`] (session-scoped) and never touch the default.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "model",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "model": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/ModelRef"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "set_default_model"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Switch the execution mode used for subsequent turns .",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "mode",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "mode": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/PermissionProfile"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "set_permission_profile"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Set product session axes (work profile × collaboration). Wire strings: work_profile = economy|balanced (legacy `delivery` reads as `balanced`); collaboration = chat|plan|goal.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "collaboration",
        "session_id",
        "type",
        "work_profile"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "collaboration": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "set_product_axes"
          ]
        },
        "work_profile": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Confirm a collaboration-plan proposal and auto-enter goal mode (K24).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "content",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "content": {
          "description": "Optional plan body; empty uses the last assistant proposal text.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "confirm_plan_to_goal"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "List project durable memory (active; optional archived) for TUI/CLI.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "include_archived": {
          "description": "Include archived (forgotten) entries.",
          "default": false,
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "list_memory"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Archive (forget) one active memory id — user-authoritative (no model).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "forget_memory"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Promote one pending candidate to durable memory. User-authoritative: this IS the consent K36 requires, so it is never model-callable.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "accept_memory"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Decline one pending candidate and suppress the same signal from being re-proposed. Distinct from [`Self::ForgetMemory`], which archives an ACTIVE entry: sending a pending id to forget did nothing at all, which is what the Web \"忽略\" button was doing.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "reject_memory"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Create a durable memory directly. The user's own command IS the authorization, so this never reaches the model and never becomes a pending candidate — it is the deterministic counterpart to the natural-language path, which can only propose.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "body",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "body": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "description": "Omitted means [`UiMemoryKind::Preference`]: `/remember` exists for \"apply this from now on\", which is what a preference is.",
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/UiMemoryKind"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "remember_memory"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Recompute and push the working-tree diff.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "request_diff"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Summarize and compact the conversation history (spec §28, §53).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "compact_context"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Start a fresh conversation: drop the session's stored message history so the next turn carries no prior context (a real \"new chat\", not a screen clear).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "clear_conversation"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Ask for the list of stored sessions (spec §52).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "request_session_list"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Ask for the session list and route the response only to the requesting session's event stream.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "requester_session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "requester_session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "request_session_list_for"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Start a FRESH session and switch the requester's view to it, leaving the current one intact in the session list.\n\nThis is what `/clear` does. Wiping the current session in place would be destructive and unrecoverable (it takes the checkpoints with it), which is why that shape needed a confirmation; starting a new session loses nothing, so it needs none.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "requester_session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "requester_session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "new_session_for"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Open a stored session, loading its transcript into the view.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "open_session"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Open a stored session on behalf of another currently displayed session. The switch event is delivered to the requester before the client moves its subscription to the target.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "requester_session_id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "requester_session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "open_session_for"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Delete a stored session.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "delete_session"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Delete a stored session and route the refreshed list to the requester.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "requester_session_id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "requester_session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "delete_session_for"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Rename a stored session (overwrite its goal/title text).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "name",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "rename_session"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Archive a stored session: it keeps its transcript but leaves the default session list.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "archive_session"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Fork a stored session: create a new session with a copy of the transcript, so an alternative direction can be explored without touching the original.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "fork_session"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Restore the conversation to a checkpoint (spec §68).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "checkpoint_id",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/CheckpointId"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/SessionId"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "restore_checkpoint"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Side question (`/btw`): single-turn answer using current session context, without tools and without appending to the transcript store. Run an explicit user shell command (`!command`) in the session's repository. USER-ORIGINATED DIRECT EXECUTION: never reaches the model, the agent loop, or the tool registry. `command` is the raw shell string after the `!` prefix.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "command",
        "session_id",
        "type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "command": {
